1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,280
This is my uncle's story. In
1982 E.C. (1989/90), he was a

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:08,460
sailor in the Ethiopian Navy.

3
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:13,560
The work was heavy. Sleep was
four hours, at most.

4
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:18,220
But on Thursday, the ship would
sail to Massawa. To him, Massawa

5
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:21,680
was like heaven.

6
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:24,800
On Tuesday, working deep in the
belly of the ship, his foot

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,620
slipped.

8
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:32,440
His ankle twisted. His arm
broke.

9
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:36,060
His commander, who loved him
like a son, told him: "You stay

10
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:39,200
here. Rest."

11
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:42,820
His heart broke. He lost all
hope; it felt like the end of

12
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:45,720
the world.

13
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:50,500
On Thursday morning, the ship
left without him.

14
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:57,200
That same Thursday, an attack by
Eritrean fighters sank the ship.

15
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:02,380
His comrades and his commander
stayed with the sea.

16
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:05,860
On Friday, he heard the news. He
calls it the day he was born

17
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:09,040
again.

18
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:12,340
The fall that broke him that day
was the hand that saved his

19
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:15,000
life.

20
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:20,420
Today he preaches the gospel. He
tells everyone one thing: "Let

21
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:24,160
God lead your life."
